 "conclusion": "Three findings survived round 140's reading of the dataset card, and each is verified here as a grid rather than a number. A: the negative block's content is less present in core than a matched positive block, in 42 of 42 representation-by-metric-by-matching cells under all 5 seeds, with 42 of 42 cells' prompt-clustered intervals excluding zero -- matched on rating magnitude, on text length and on rater count separately, over token, stemmed-token and character-trigram representations, under Jaccard, Dice, containment, idf-weighted and min-overlap. This is the one place the card's stated NEGATE step is not visible in the artifact. B: the shared component of what raters call important is ICC 0.2698 at n>=4; ICC 0.2697 at n>=5; ICC 0.2691 at n>=10, against a rater-style null of 0.0006, and Krippendorff's alpha and the median rater-pair correlation agree; the card says core 'often reflects the biases of dominant perspectives' and this is that statement's size. C: 63.5% of rated criteria carry exactly one rating and EXACTLY ZERO carry two or three, which the card does not mention and which is a protocol signature rather than a sampling curve. VERIFIED: True.",
